      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Ah, the E15 error code, a pesky little goblin in the world of Bosch dishwashers. First, let's tackle the leak sensor, a mischievous goblin that loves to hide in the nooks and crannies. To check it, you'll need to locate the sensor, usually found near the door latch or the bottom of the dishwasher. Gently remove the cover, and there you have it, the sensor. If it's dirty, give it a good wipe with a damp cloth, but don't let it get too wet, or you'll be dealing with a soggy goblin. If the sensor is damaged, you'll need to replace it, but don't worry, it's not as tricky as it sounds.\n\nNow, onto the bottom part, the goblin's lair. To dry it out, you'll need to remove the bottom rack and any dishes that might be hiding there. Then, use a towel to soak up any water, and if you're feeling particularly brave, you can also use a hairdryer on a low setting to dry it out faster. Just be careful not to burn yourself or your precious dishes. Once the lair is dry, put the rack back in place and run a short cycle to ensure everything is back to",
